{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1nwsjXejMqdNuBf9teN", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I did not sign off. I found two defects, both filed, and I have not cleared the areas. The sign-off tool only accepts PASS, which would be wrong with these open.\n\n**Filed and confirmed**\n- **Create deck with \"::\"** (nested deck dialog): with \"::\" in the Name field, Create is enabled. Tapping it shows \"Deck created\" and makes a deck named \"blank\". A blank or spaces-only name correctly keeps Create disabled. The developer confirmed and logged this one.\n\n**Filed, not reproduced by the developer**\n- **Note type not kept in Add note**: I saw this three times. Choosing a type, pressing Back and reopening Add showed \"Basic\" instead. A later reopen then showed the earlier choice, and one later attempt showed the chosen type correctly. The developer could not reproduce it from my steps, so the behaviour is intermittent. The Add deck also showed \"blank::blank\" after the \"::\" deck was created.\n\n**Checked and working**\n- **Set due date**: OK is disabled for an empty day, a day over 36501 and a reversed range (12–9). Cancel leaves the due date unchanged. Setting mesa to a 3–9 range moved it to 2026-11-17, which is in range.\n- **Statistics**: Today, Future Due, Reviews, Calendar and Card Counts agree with the deck list. After one review, Today reads \"Studied 1 card\" and Card Counts totals 4 for Spanish and 7 for the collection. The charts survive rotation.\n- **Nested deck**: \"Spanish::Verbs\" creates a child deck under Spanish. Whitespace-only names are rejected.\n- **Notes**: an edit to comer's Back field and its \"verb\" tag persisted after saving and reopening.\n\n**Not covered**\n- The French deck's statistics and the undo paths for due-date changes.\n- The Day field silently drops \"-\" and \".\" (typing \"-1\" gives \"1\", \"1.5\" gives \"15\"). I did not file this because it may be intended.\n\n**Cleanup needed**\n- My \"::\" test created a deck named \"blank\" that is still in the collection. I did not delete it, because I was told not to change data beyond what testing needs. The \"Verbs\" deck under Spanish was created during testing and is also still there.\n\nBoth open items need a decision from the developer or you. I'm ready to retest the Add note type behaviour, or to cover the French statistics and undo paths, if you want more before release."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1805, "cache_read_input_tokens": 139427, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1805}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ddf15106-5c66-4b1d-bfb9-b00d73fa5754", "uuid": "ae2d21be-0de6-4903-8894-f84b95a17d13", "timestamp": "2026-11-13T23:26:57.966Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1nwsTAeQza7kAqc3nHH"}
